Q: Corrupt object variables in C++ for ESP32 A: <p>You are likely instantiating your ProximitySensor objects as local variables (on the stack) inside a function like setup(), but then storing pointers to them in a global list or a class member.</p>
<p>Try to define your sensors outside of any function. This places them in the Data/BSS segment, where they live forever and don't fragment the heap.</p>
<pre><code>// Globally defined
ProximitySensor frontSensor(12, 13, 0); 

void setup() {
    myRobot.addSensor(&amp;frontSensor); // Safe: address never changes
}
</code></pre>
<p>You used <code>const int pin_trig;</code>. Somebody might think const makes a variable &quot;permanent.&quot; It doesn't. const only tells the compiler to prevent your code from changing the value. It provides zero protection against the underlying memory being reclaimed and overwritten by the hardware.</p>

Q: How to change the background color of a TButton component with code in Delphi FMX? A: <p>Here's an example I wrote to make a red button with a green border:</p>
<pre><code>Button3.ApplyStyleLookup;
var LBg := Button3.FindStyleResource('background');

if LBg = nil then Exit;
if not (LBg is TFmxObject) then Exit;

var LRect := TRectangle.Create(TFmxObject(LBg));
LRect.Name := Button3.Name + '_background';
LRect.HitTest := False;
LRect.Align := TAlignLayout.Client;
LRect.Fill.Kind := TBrushKind.Solid;
LRect.Fill.Color := TAlphaColorRec.Red;
LRect.Stroke.Kind := TBrushKind.Solid;
LRect.Stroke.Color := TAlphaColorRec.Green;
LRect.Stroke.Thickness := 4;
TFmxObject(LBg).AddObject(LRect);
</code></pre>
<p>This code will take a <code>TButton</code> on my form (<code>Button3</code> in this case), and add a <code>TRectangle</code> onto the <code>background</code> style resource of it, and then with that <code>TRectangle</code> you can do whatever you want such as set the <code>Fill.Color</code> to red or set the <code>Stroke.Color</code> (border) to green.</p>
<p>Remember to set <code>HitTest</code> to <code>False</code>. If you don't do this, then you won't be able to click on the button anymore.</p>
