Q: how to add header to fetch GET method A: <p>You can try it out this way,</p>
<pre><code>var myHeaders = new Headers();
myHeaders.append(&quot;User-Agent&quot;, &quot;PostmanRuntime/7.29.2&quot;);

var requestOptions = {
  method: 'GET',
  headers: myHeaders,
  redirect: 'follow'
};

fetch(&quot;http://api.github.com/users&quot;, requestOptions)
  .then(response =&gt; response.text())
  .then(result =&gt; console.log(result))
  .catch(error =&gt; console.log('error', error));
</code></pre>
<p>As I am a Frontend Developer I use postman to handle and structure all sorts of fetching code. you can try it out as well. Might solve your issue.</p>
